## 1. iStaffing Scope

iStaffing is the staffing, scheduling, clinician-patient matching, training readiness, credential readiness, and staffing automation module inside CIHH-App.

### Module Boundary

iStaffing covers:
- Clinician Profile management
- Patient Profile management
- Clinician-Patient Connection management
- Calendar surface for shift visibility (open, filled, pending coverage, cancelled)
- Training readiness tracking
- Credential readiness tracking
- Future AI-assisted staffing recommendations (Step 3 — planned only)
- Future AI-assisted staffing support via multi-model orchestration (Step 3 — planned only)

### Agency Operational Context

| Parameter | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| Agency | Care Indeed Home Health (Bay Area) |
| Active Census | ~150 patients across 60-day episodes |
| Weekly Visit Volume | ~1,200 visits/week |
| Clinician Pool | 400+ clinicians and caregivers |
| Service Area | San Mateo County, parts of Alameda and Contra Costa |
| Scheduling System | AlayaCare (EVV-compliant) |
| Payer Mix | Medicare, Medi-Cal, Private Insurance |
| Scheduling Staff | VCCs (Virtual Care Coordinators) |

### Weighted Caseload Formula

```
Weighted Caseload = (L3-L4 × 1.0) + (L2 × 0.75) + (L1 × 0.5)
Hard cap: 40 points per ACCM
Near Full band: 36–39 points → flagged for review before new patient intake
At Cap: 40 points → no new patients assigned
```

