## 8. Validation Requirements

### 8.1 The 14 Required Validation Checks

Every staffing proposal in Step 3 must pass all 14 checks. iStaffing Validator is responsible.

| # | Check | Type | Blocking? |
|---|-------|------|-----------|
| 1 | Availability check | Hard constraint | Yes — blocks if unavailable |
| 2 | Credential check | Hard constraint | Yes — blocks if invalid/expired |
| 3 | License check | Hard constraint | Yes — blocks if expired |
| 4 | Competency check | Hard or soft | Hard if isRequired=true; soft otherwise |
| 5 | Required training check | Hard constraint | Yes — blocks if training not current |
| 6 | Patient restriction check | Hard constraint | Yes — blocks if hard restriction active |
| 7 | Facility restriction check | Hard constraint | Yes — blocks if facility restriction active |
| 8 | Conflict check | Hard constraint | Yes — blocks if conflict detected |
| 9 | Overtime check | Hard constraint | Yes — blocks if CA OT threshold exceeded |
| 10 | Rest-period check | Hard constraint | Yes — blocks if rest period violated |
| 11 | Continuity-of-care check | Soft | No — scored; logged if continuity break |
| 12 | Fairness/workload balancing check | Soft | No — scored; flagged if severe disparity |
| 13 | Approval requirement check | Meta | Determines if human gate is required |
| 14 | Audit readiness check | Meta | Blocks if required audit fields missing |

### 8.2 Validation Outcome States

| Outcome | Meaning |
|---------|---------|
| validation_failed | At least one hard constraint check failed; proposal is blocked |
| validation_passed | All hard constraints passed; soft scores calculated; proposal ready for approval gate |

### 8.3 Credential Expiry Enforcement Rules

- `valid` → `expiringSoon` at 30 days before expiration (configurable threshold)
- `expiringSoon` → `expired` at expiration date
- `expired` → clinician is ineligible for any assignment requiring this credential
- No human may override an expired required credential (per 42 CFR §484.115)
- System BLOCKS, does not warn. There is no "assign anyway" option for expired credentials.

