## 9. Approval Requirements

### 9.1 Human-in-the-Loop Requirements

All staffing proposals must pass through a human approval gate before any production schedule record is written. This requirement is non-negotiable and applies in Step 3.

| Condition | Required Approver |
|-----------|-----------------|
| First-time clinician-patient connection | ACCM / Clinical Manager |
| Override of iStaffing Scheduler recommendation | Clinical Manager (§484.115 qualified) |
| High-acuity (L3-L4) patient — new assignment | Clinical Manager |
| Bias-flagged proposal | Clinical Manager (must review and document) |
| Expanded radius (>25 miles) | Scheduler or Clinical Manager |
| PRN or overtime authorization | Clinical Manager or Admin |
| Expired required credential | BLOCKED — no approval possible |

### 9.2 Approval Documentation Requirements

| # | Requirement |
|---|-------------|
| A.1 | approvedBy field must be populated with the UUID of the approving human |
| A.2 | approvedAt timestamp must be recorded |
| A.3 | approvalRationale text must be provided for all flagged or override approvals |
| A.4 | Approver must hold qualifying credentials per 42 CFR §484.115 for clinical approvals |
| A.5 | Approver role must be logged in the audit entry at time of approval |
| A.6 | The review must be meaningful — the approver must have access to match score, match factor breakdown, bias flags, accommodation check results, and any risk flags |

### 9.3 Meaningful Review Requirement

Per FEHA ADS regulations and 42 CFR §484, human review must be meaningful — not a rubber stamp. The system must present the following to the approver at review time:

- Ranked candidates (if applicable)
- Match scores and factor breakdowns
- Bias check summary
- Accommodation conflict check results
- Risk flags
- Applicable citation card

### 9.4 Approval Actions Requiring Supervisor/Admin Level

| Action | Required Approver |
|--------|------------------|
| Remove a hard restriction/block | Admin (safety concern — requires investigation) |
| Authorize PRN/overtime assignment | Clinical Manager or Admin |
| Approve expanded radius (>25 miles) | Scheduler or Clinical Manager |
| Override bias-flagged assignment | Clinical Manager (must document bias concern evaluation) |

