## 12. ADS / FEHA Future-Readiness Requirements

Future AI-assisted staffing recommendations may be treated as Automated Decision System (ADS) decision-support activity under California FEHA. The system must preserve the data fields, terminology, and audit-ready structure needed for future ADS compliance, but early implementation must not perform active matching, autonomous scheduling, or production staffing decisions.

### 12.1 ADS Compliance Requirements

| # | Requirement |
|---|-------------|
| ADS.1 | All AI-generated recommendation outputs must carry the required disclaimer |
| ADS.2 | Accommodation fields (religious, ADA, pregnancy, FMLA) are hard constraints — no override |
| ADS.3 | Disparate impact monitoring (Layer 3 bias check) must run before any human review |
| ADS.4 | Bias flags must be surfaced to the human approver before approval |
| ADS.5 | Every assignment audit entry must document the bias check result |
| ADS.6 | Override documentation is required when a human deviates from the AI recommendation |
| ADS.7 | Clinician demographic fields (race, sex, age) are stored for bias audit only — never used in matching |
| ADS.8 | Language match factor must be monitored for disparate mileage burden |
| ADS.9 | Feedback score factor must be bias-audited before use in matching |
| ADS.10 | Monthly disparate impact reports must be generated (Step 3) |
| ADS.11 | Clinician appeal process must be documented and implemented (Step 3) |

### 12.2 Required Disclaimer Text

All iStaffing AI-generated recommendation outputs must include this disclaimer verbatim:

> "AI-assisted recommendation. Assignment subject to clinical manager review and approval per 42 CFR §484 and agency policy. This tool does not make final staffing decisions."

### 12.3 Regulatory Framework (All Apply Simultaneously)

| Regulation | Authority | iStaffing Impact |
|------------|-----------|----------------|
| CA FEHA ADS Regulations | CA Civil Rights Council | Applies to scheduling decisions about US-based clinicians |
| 42 CFR Part 484 (CoP) | CMS Federal | Clinical manager must approve; system cannot make final assignment |
| Title VII / ADA / ADEA | EEOC | Disparate impact rules apply to US-based workforce scheduling |
| CA Labor Law | State | Daily OT after 8hrs, weekly after 40hrs must be modeled |

### 12.4 Terminology Requirements for ADS

**Use:**
- "future AI-assisted staffing recommendations"
- "future AI-assisted staffing support"
- "decision-support"
- "human approval gates"
- "validation before execution"

**Do NOT Use:**
- "automated staffing decision"
- "autonomous scheduling"
- "iStaffing automatically assigns clinicians"
- "active AI matching"
- "production scheduling automation"

