## Appendix A: Escalation Triggers (Consequence Engine — Step 3 Design)

These triggers define when iStaffing must surface alerts to human operators. They are documented here for Step 3 planning and must not be activated in Steps 1 or 2.

| Trigger | Action | Source |
|---------|--------|--------|
| Preventable cancellation rate > 30%/week | Escalate to CEO with root cause | QA/PI Playbook |
| Patient with 3+ cancellations/week | ACCM notification, at-risk flag | QA/PI Playbook |
| Uncoded cancellations not corrected in 24hr | Escalate to Care Management Director | QA/PI Playbook |
| Visit delivery < 95% | Red flag, weekly brief required | ACCM Tracker V2 |
| Caregiver no-call/no-show | Route to CG Success Supervisor (NEVER ACCM) | Role Separation Policy |
| Weighted caseload hits 40 | Hard cap, no new patients | Facility/B2B Playbook |
| Caseload 36-39 | Flagged Near Full, review before new assignment | Facility/B2B Playbook |

